481	--- Guide for required-field-feedback ---
482	# Required Field Feedback
483	
484	## The Problem
485	Marking required fields with an error state immediately upon page load can be confusing. Ideally, a required field should only look "invalid" if the user has attempted to fill it out and failed.
486	
487	## The Solution
488	The `:user-invalid` pseudo-class solves this perfectly. For a required field, it will not match on page load. It will only match if:
489	1.  The user interacts with the field (e.g., types a character and deletes it) and then leaves it (blur), leaving it empty.
490	2.  The user attempts to submit the form while the field is empty.
491	
492	### Implementation Strategy
493	
494	1.  **HTML Constraint**: Add the `required` attribute to your inputs.
495	2.  **Visual Feedback**: Use `:user-invalid` to style the border red and show a "Required" helper text.
496	3.  **Timing**: Rely on the browser's native timing for visual feedback. You don't need `onBlur` handlers to add a `touched` class anymore, though some JavaScript is still needed to sync ARIA attributes (see below).
497	4.  **Error Text**: Show visible error text with the error styling, so the error isn't shown by color alone. Start each message with an error icon that has a text alternative such as "Error" (the safest choice), or word every message as an error, for example "Name is required.", and use the same approach for every error in the form.
498	5.  **Error Link**: List the error message in the field's `aria-describedby` only while the field is invalid, so screen readers read it with the field. A reference in the markup would read the hidden message from page load. The script in section 3 does this for each field whose `data-error` attribute is set to its error message's `id`.
499	
500	## Implementation Guide
501	
502	### 1. HTML Structure
503	```html
504	<form id="feedback-form">
505	  <div class="field">
506	    <label for="full-name">Full Name</label>
507	    <!-- Set data-error to the error message's id. The aria-invalid script lists that id in aria-describedby while the field is invalid. -->
508	    <input
509	      type="text"
510	      id="full-name"
511	      name="full-name"
512	      required
513	      data-error="name-error"
514	    >
515	    <!-- MANDATORY: Include an icon or distinct non-color indicator alongside error text -->
516	    <div id="name-error" class="error-msg">
517	      <span role="img" aria-label="Error">❌</span> This field is required.
518	    </div>
519	  </div>
520	</form>
521	```
522	
523	### 2. CSS
524	```css
525	.error-msg {
526	  display: none;
